ExtinctOS
===========

Getting started
---------------

To get started with Android/ExtinctOS, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

To initialize your local repository using the ExtinctOS trees, use a command like this:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/ExtinctOS/manifest.git -b bka --git-lfs
```
Or If you wish to save some system space and don't care about repo history depths:
```
repo init --depth=1 --no-repo-verify --git-lfs -u https://github.com/ExtinctOS/manifest.git -b bka -g default,-mips,-darwin,-notdefault
```
Then to sync up:
```
repo sync -c --no-clone-bundle --no-tags --optimized-fetch --prune --force-sync -j$(nproc --all)
```

